Feature:

Background: This executes once per feature file
	Given these properties
		|portal.release|true|
		|portal.upstream|true|
		|testray.main.component.name|Security|

Setup: This executes before each scenario 
	Given TestCase set Up Portal Instance

Scenario: CAS Smoke
Priority: 4
	Given these properties
		|test.name.skip.portal.instance|Login#CASSmoke|
	When these properties
		|web.plugins.includes|cas-web|
	And these variables
		|portalURL|TestPropsUtil#get('portal.url')|
	And these variables
		|userEmailAddress|userea@liferay.com|
	And these variables
		|userFirstName|userfn|
	And these variables
		|userLastName|userln|
	And these variables
		|userScreenName|usersn|
	And User first Login PG
	And ProductMenu goto Control Panel Users
		|portlet|Users and Organizations|
	And User add CP
		|userEmailAddress|${userEmailAddress}|
		|userFirstName|${userFirstName}|
		|userLastName|${userLastName}|
		|userScreenName|${userScreenName}|
	And ProductMenu goto Control Panel Users
		|portlet|Users and Organizations|
	And User edit Password CP
		|userEmailAddress|${userEmailAddress}|
		|userScreenName|${userScreenName}|
	And ProductMenu goto Control Panel Configuration
		|portlet|Instance Settings|
	And PortalSettings edit Configuration Authentication General
		|authenticationMethod|By Screen Name|
	And PortalSettings edit Configuration Authentication CAS
		|casLoginURL|${portalURL}/cas-web/login|
		|casLogoutURL|${portalURL}/cas-web/logout|
		|casServerURL|${portalURL}/cas-web|
		|casServiceURL|${portalURL}/c/portal/login|
	And User logout PG
	And User view Logged Out With CAS Enabled PG
	And User login User With CAS Enabled PG
		|userScreenName|${userScreenName}|
	And User logout PG
	Then User login User With CAS Enabled PG
		|userScreenName|test|
Scenario: Facebook SSO Smoke
Priority: 4
	Given these properties
		|test.name.skip.portal.instance|Login#FacebookSSOSmoke|
	When these variables
		|facebookApplicationID||
	And these variables
		|facebookApplicationSecret||
	And these variables
		|facebookEmail||
	And these variables
		|facebookPassword||
	And User first Login PG
	And TestCase get Site Name
##########################################################
The Poshi return element is not supported in the readable syntax. Please update this test.
##########################################################
		|siteName|${siteName}|
	And ProductMenu goto Control Panel Configuration
		|portlet|Instance Settings|
	And Panel expand Panel
		|panelHeading|Authentication|
	And PortalSettingsNavigator goto Authentication Facebook
	And PortalSettings edit Configuration Authentication Facebook
		|facebookApplicationID|${facebookApplicationID}|
		|facebookApplicationSecret|${facebookApplicationSecret}|
	And User logout PG
	And User login User With Facebook SSO Enabled PG
		|facebookEmail|${facebookEmail}|
		|facebookPassword|${facebookPassword}|
		|siteName|${siteName}|
	And User logout User PG
	Then User login PG
		|password|test|
		|userEmailAddress|test@liferay.com|
		|userScreenName|usersn|
Scenario: Google SSO Smoke
Priority: 4
	Given these properties
		|test.name.skip.portal.instance|Login#GoogleSSOSmoke|
	When these variables
		|googleClientID||
	And these variables
		|googleClientSecret||
	And these variables
		|userEmailAddress||
	And these variables
		|userPassword||
	And User first Login PG
	And TestCase get Site Name
##########################################################
The Poshi return element is not supported in the readable syntax. Please update this test.
##########################################################
		|siteName|${siteName}|
	And ProductMenu goto Control Panel Configuration
		|portlet|Instance Settings|
	And Panel expand Panel
		|panelHeading|Authentication|
	And PortalSettingsNavigator goto Authentication Google
	And PortalSettings enable Google SSOCP
		|googleClientID|${googleClientID}|
		|googleClientSecret|${googleClientSecret}|
	And User logout PG
	And User login User With Google SSO Enabled PG
		|siteName|${siteName}|
		|userEmailAddress|${userEmailAddress}|
		|userPassword|${userPassword}|
	And User logout PG
	Then User login User PG
		|password|test|
		|userEmailAddress|test@liferay.com|
Scenario: Login
Priority: 4
	Given these properties
		|test.name.skip.portal.instance|Login#Login|
	When User first Login PG
	And User logout PG
	Then User login PG
Scenario: Login First Time
Priority: 4
	Given SignIn sign In
	When SignIn agree To Terms Of Use
	And SignIn set Password Reminder
	Then Smoke view Welcome Page
Scenario: Open ID Smoke
Priority: 4
	Given these properties
		|test.name.skip.portal.instance|Login#OpenIDSmoke|
	When these variables
		|openIDPassword|TestPropsUtil#get('openid.password')|
	And these variables
		|openIDUsername|TestPropsUtil#get('openid.username')|
	And User first Login PG
	And ProductMenu goto Control Panel Configuration
		|portlet|Instance Settings|
	And Panel expand Panel
		|panelHeading|Authentication|
	And PortalSettingsNavigator goto Authentication Open ID
	And PortalSettings enable Open IDCP
	And User logout PG
	And User login User With Open ID Enabled PG
		|openIDPassword|${openIDPassword}|
		|openIDUsername|${openIDUsername}|
		|password|test|
		|userEmailAddress|userea2@liferay.com|
		|userName|userfn2|
	And User logout PG
	Then User login User PG
		|password|test|
		|userEmailAddress|test@liferay.com|
Scenario: Open SSO Smoke
Priority: 5
	Given these properties
		|openam.enabled|true|
	When these properties
		|test.name.skip.portal.instance|Login#OpenSSOSmoke|
	And Navigator open Specific URL
		|url|http://test.able.com:8080/openam|
	And AntCommand the value 'run-openam-tools' at locator 'build-test-authentication.xml'
	And PortalSettings refresh Open AM Setup
		|pauseCount|0|
	And User first Login PG
	And ProductMenu goto Control Panel Configuration
		|portlet|Instance Settings|
	And Pause at locator '30000'
	And Panel expand Panel
		|panelHeading|Authentication|
	And PortalSettingsNavigator goto Authentication Open SSO
	And PortalSettings configure Open SSO
		|OpenSSOLoginURL|http://test.able.com:8080/openam/UI/Login?goto=http://www.able.com:8080/c/portal/login|
		|OpenSSOLogoutURL|http://test.able.com:8080/openam/UI/Logout?goto=http://www.able.com:8080/web/guest/home|
		|OpenSSOServiceURL|http://test.able.com:8080/openam|
	And PortalSettingsNavigator goto Authentication Open SSO
	And PortalSettings test Open SSO Connection
	And User logout PG
	Then User login User With Open SSO Enabled PG
		|hostsURL|http://www.able.com:8080|
		|password|password|
		|userScreenName|test|
Scenario: Token Based SSO Smoke
Priority: 5
	Given these properties
		|test.name.skip.portal.instance|Login#TokenBasedSSOSmoke|
	When User first Login PG
	And ProductMenu goto Control Panel Configuration
		|portlet|System Settings|
	And SystemSettings goto Category
		|category|Foundation|
	And SystemSettings view Configuration
		|configurationName|Token Based SSO|
	And SystemSettings enable Setting
		|checkboxSetting|ENABLED_CHECKBOX|
	And PortletEntry save
	And User logout PG
	Then AntCommand the value 'verify-token-based-login' at locator 'build-test-authentication.xml'